{
  "tema": 5726,
  "slug": "subjuntivo-presente-zar",
  "titulo": "Conjugate -zar verbs (z > c) in the present subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Utilizar → utilice: z can't stand in front of e.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Verbs ending in -zar change z to c in every form of the present subjunctive: utilice, utilices, utilicemos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs ending in **-zar** change the **z** to **c** in the present subjunctive. The reason is spelling: in Spanish, **z** almost never comes before **e** or **i**, so before **e** it becomes **c**. The sound doesn't change."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**-zar** → **-c-**",
            "**-e, -es, -e, -emos, -en**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "utilizar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "utilice"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "utilices"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "utilice"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "utilicemos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "utilicen"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The change is in **every form**. Other verbs like this: **abrazar** → **abrace**, **alcanzar** → **alcance**, **cruzar** → **cruce**, **organizar** → **organice**, **analizar** → **analice**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Some **-zar** verbs also have a stem change, like **empezar** → **empiece**: see [[5990|-zar verbs with e > ie]]."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **z** and **e** never hold hands in Spanish. **C** steps in between them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ten cuidado cuando ==utilices== la sierra.",
              "en": "Be careful when you use the saw."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que los niños ==crucen== la calle con cuidado.",
              "en": "I hope the kids cross the street carefully."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡No me ==abraces== tan fuerte!",
              "en": "Don't hug me so tight!"
            },
            {
              "es": "No me gusta que ==utilices== mis herramientas.",
              "en": "I don't like you using my tools."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==utilicen== el huerto comunitario.",
              "en": "I hope you use the community garden."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ojalá que ==alcancemos== la ola.",
              "en": "I hope we catch the wave."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
